    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640-a4">

                <pb facs="0728" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg648"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woël to Mr. Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Gonaives, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is my duty to advise you that the
                    bearer, steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Valencia</hi>, landed some arms and
                    ammunition for Mr. Firmin. They are sent by Mr. Jimenez and consigned to R.
                    Sanchez, a Cuban citizen.</p>
                <p>It is also rumored that the next steamer will bring us some paper money for the
                    Artibonite revolution which will be made legal tender. What do you think of such
                    a money if they do not succeed? May we take the money in our trade without any
                    risk?</p>
                <p>Your valuable answer will greatly oblige yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. William Woël.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
